{"batchcomplete":true,"query":{"pages":[{"pageid":10886610,"ns":0,"title":"Trivialism","extract":"Trivialism is the logical theory that all statements (also known as propositions) are true and, consequently, that all contradictions of the form \"p and not p\" (e.g. the ball is red and not red) are true.","description":"Logical theory","descriptionsource":"local"}]}}